1
00:00:00,267 --> 00:00:03,612
Here's how to reverse engineer QuotaPath from a written spec.

2
00:00:03,667 --> 00:00:08,219
We gave Claude one Markdown file, and checked twenty-four things in a real browser.

3
00:00:08,274 --> 00:00:10,194
Here's what passed, and what broke.

4
00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:15,134
The spec copies the part of QuotaPath a small sales team actually uses.

5
00:00:15,192 --> 00:00:18,045
Plans with tiers, and an accelerator above quota.

6
00:00:18,103 --> 00:00:21,248
Closed deals, with an optional split between two reps.

7
00:00:21,306 --> 00:00:24,799
A statement for every rep that shows the math, line by line.

8
00:00:24,858 --> 00:00:27,536
And one finance approval that locks the month.

9
00:00:28,333 --> 00:00:31,681
The core rule is that tiers are marginal, like tax brackets.

10
00:00:31,737 --> 00:00:34,247
Cy's monthly quota is sixty thousand dollars.

11
00:00:34,303 --> 00:00:36,758
His first thirty thousand pays five percent.

12
00:00:36,814 --> 00:00:39,492
The next twenty-eight thousand pays ten percent.

13
00:00:39,548 --> 00:00:41,891
Above quota, the accelerator pays fifteen.

14
00:00:41,947 --> 00:00:47,637
So his October commission is four thousand three hundred dollars, and his statement shows every slice.

15
00:00:48,433 --> 00:00:51,078
Claude built it in four phases, one prompt each.

16
00:00:51,133 --> 00:00:53,503
The foundation, with reps, plans and deals.

17
00:00:53,558 --> 00:00:55,487
The calculation and the statements.

18
00:00:55,542 --> 00:00:58,407
Approval, locking, clawbacks and the payroll export.

19
00:00:58,462 --> 00:01:02,319
Then what reps see, with their own statement and a what-if calculator.

20
00:01:02,375 --> 00:01:07,058
After every phase, the acceptance checks ran in a real browser, from fresh seed data.

21
00:01:07,867 --> 00:01:08,936
Here's what it built.

22
00:01:08,987 --> 00:01:13,619
The payouts screen shows each rep's quota, attainment, commission and payout for the month.

23
00:01:13,670 --> 00:01:18,608
Each statement walks through every deal, tier by tier, including a clawback for a cancelled deal.

24
00:01:18,659 --> 00:01:23,190
The what-if calculator shows a rep what one more deal would pay, without saving anything.

25
00:01:23,241 --> 00:01:25,787
And reps check their own statement on their phone.

26
00:01:26,600 --> 00:01:32,660
In the final run, on a fresh database, all twenty-four checks passed, along with forty-eight automated tests.

27
00:01:33,467 --> 00:01:35,571
But the more useful result is what broke.

28
00:01:35,622 --> 00:01:37,624
The build exposed ten gaps in the spec.

29
00:01:37,675 --> 00:01:39,369
Places where Claude had to guess.

30
00:01:39,420 --> 00:01:43,167
Sign-in had to match each person by email, but people had no email field.

31
00:01:43,218 --> 00:01:52,148
Recalculating an approved month left out a deal cancelled after approval, so August came to eight thousand, eight hundred and sixty dollars instead of ten thousand and sixty.

32
00:01:52,199 --> 00:01:54,868
And the what-if split could mean either rep's share.

33
00:01:54,919 --> 00:01:56,716
Every gap is now fixed in the spec.

34
00:01:57,500 --> 00:02:00,684
Passing every check isn't the same as production-ready.

35
00:02:00,742 --> 00:02:08,094
We didn't test real sign-in, two people saving at the same moment, importing the export into a real payroll system, or hosting.

36
00:02:08,152 --> 00:02:11,162
Those are yours to check before a team relies on it.

37
00:02:11,967 --> 00:02:13,252
So is it worth building?

38
00:02:13,306 --> 00:02:18,823
QuotaPath Growth is thirty-five dollars per user per month, plus a monthly platform fee, billed yearly.

39
00:02:18,877 --> 00:02:21,341
Every rep, manager and admin counts as a user.

40
00:02:21,395 --> 00:02:25,734
If you need CRM sync, draws or team roll-up plans, QuotaPath is worth paying for.

41
00:02:25,787 --> 00:02:32,055
If you have a few reps on one or two plans, you mostly need the tiers, the statements, and a month that stays locked.

42
00:02:32,867 --> 00:02:33,875
The spec is free.

43
00:02:33,935 --> 00:02:41,056
The data model, fifteen rules, seed data, four phase prompts, and all twenty-four checks, with the ten fixes already in.

44
00:02:41,115 --> 00:02:43,786
Find it at personal software factory dot com.
